  "text": "UNCLE ANDY AMESS • AUNT TiLL.\nMonday, October 13, 1958\nAssociate Holes In One\nAt Royal Canberra\nMrs. Pat Byrne holed in one at the seventh at Royal Can-\nberra yesterday, in the course of the Canadian stableford mixed\nfoursomes.\nbv R. D.\nThe Competition Was on month medal for S. Taun. cd. co\ned consistently over the 18\nSatundau\nWallace (\nof 36\npoi\nback fron\nMiss M.\nBROTHERHOOD OF S. LAURENCE\npoints.\nScores\n36,\nFrom THE REV. G. KENNEDY TUCKER\nTelephone: Carrum Downs 236\nSUPERIOR'S LODGE\nCARRUM DOWNS\nVICTORIA\nHorgan (\nand Miss\n31,\nB3\nByrne (18\nCrombie\nand Mrs.\n30,\nN.\n(8)\n29\nJ.\nTurnb\nByrne\nan\n(11)\n29.\nA\nthe\ntwo\nout,\n(Train to Frankston)\n6th June, 1956.\nC. H. McFadzen, Esq • ,\nDepartment of Shippin & Transport,\nMELBOURNE.\nDear w. O.,\nIt was indeed nice of you to write\nto me concerning the honor Her Majesty has\nbeen pleased to confer upon me.\nYour letter takes me back to those\nhappy and interesting days with the C.c.S.\nI do hope that you and the boys will\nbe able to visit me here.\nI fear I can offer\nnothing stronger than tea, but I will see that\nit really is tea!\nWith again my thanks,\nYours sincerely,\n9. Kennedy Lucken\nSRANDMA WILSON, AUNT TILL a UNChE ANDY\nALICE LINDA -ErELyN\n'GRAHAmSTON' 1916-1918.\nLAVE NORRIS WITH LADIES PROM FLEM. PASS\nInA BASTER S-101 STAN HASTINGS",
